cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the codebook in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "CDS-Skill: a cognitive dissonance simulation skill for LLM agents"
abstract: >-
  A pluggable agent skill that turns a conflict between an agent's own committed
  position and incoming information into a detectable, auditable and reproducible
  event, then routes it to an explicit response strategy. Perception is performed
  by the host language model and emitted as a structured signal packet; the index,
  the dissonance gate, evidence scoring, strategy routing, card rendering and audit
  logging are deterministic and dependency-free. The skill reports two channels --
  dissonance, which requires a freely chosen and self-relevant stance, and
  indeterminacy, which does not -- and offers both an epistemic-recalibration
  repertoire and a human-typical dissonance-reduction repertoire.
type: software
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-09-10"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - cognitive dissonance
  - large language models
  - LLM agents
  - agent skills
  - human factors
  - behaviour simulation
  - reproducibility
repository-code: "https://github.com/Penghhhh/cognitivedissonance-agent-skill"
url: "https://github.com/Penghhhh/cognitivedissonance-agent-skill"

